.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt PKG-STATE 5
.Os "pkg-mgr 0.1.0 experimental"
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg-state
.Nd private staged-package records and requested roots
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Package state records describe observed files beneath an initialized private root.
They do not grant capability authority, activate services or describe a live system
installation.
The state helper requires a single writer and a caller-controlled filesystem.
.Pp
The authoritative files are
.Pa state/packages/NAME.tsv
and
.Pa state/world .
There is no authoritative database or generated view cache.
Registration leaves world unchanged.
Use the package commands rather than editing generated package records.
.Sh RECORD FORMAT
New records use pkg-state-v2.
Fields are separated by literal tabs; writers terminate rows with newline.
The first three rows are:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
format<TAB>pkg-state-v2
package<TAB>NAME<TAB>VERSION
build-record<TAB>SHA256
.Ed
.Pp
SHA256 is the 64-character lowercase hexadecimal hash of the canonical embedded
build record.
The next 19 rows have the shape
.Ql evidence<TAB>KEY<TAB>VALUE
in the order specified below.
Dependencies follow evidence, then files follow dependencies.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li dependency<TAB>NAME
A package identifier, in strictly increasing byte order with no duplicates.
The named package must already be registered, or be the candidate itself.
Cycles are allowed; no version constraints or solver are implemented.
.It Li file<TAB>SHA256<TAB>SIZE<TAB>PATH<TAB>MODE
A regular-file row.
Paths are in strictly increasing byte order with no duplicates.
SIZE is zero or a decimal number without leading zeros.
MODE is four octal digits from 0000 through 0777.
SHA256 covers file bytes; the mode is a separate local observation.
.El
.Pp
Unknown, missing, duplicate, reordered or malformed rows fail validation.
Evidence identity must match the package header.
Fingerprints are recomputed when records are loaded; hash consistency alone does
not establish publisher authenticity or reproducibility.
.Sh BUILD EVIDENCE
Keys appear in this exact order.
All values are nonempty printable ASCII.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li record_type
Must be build.
.It Li repo_origin
Advisory repository origin.
.It Li namespace
Advisory namespace.
.It Li package_name
Must equal NAME in the package header.
.It Li version
Must equal VERSION in the package header.
.It Li recipe_path
Advisory recipe reference.
.It Li recipe_revision
Advisory recipe revision.
.It Li source_hash_alg
Must be sha256.
.It Li source_hash
64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.
.It Li manifest_hash
The prefix sha256: followed by 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.
Bound to canonical file-content manifest rows.
.It Li materials_ref
Advisory materials reference.
.It Li material_path
Advisory material path.
.It Li sbom_ref
Advisory software bill of materials reference.
.It Li builder_label
Advisory builder label.
.It Li phase_label
Advisory build phase label.
.It Li command_label
Advisory command label; never evaluated as shell code.
.It Li provenance_confidence
Must be advisory.
.It Li verification_result
Must be warn.
.It Li result_label
Must be reproducible-build-success-not-proven.
.El
.Pp
Registration does not rerun a build or resolve these advisory references.
The schema is implemented by
.Pa mk/state-schema.awk ;
the state helper additionally verifies manifest/build fingerprints, the package
graph and logical ownership conflicts.
.Sh IDENTIFIERS AND PATHS
Package names and versions start with an ASCII letter or digit, followed by
letters, digits, dot, underscore, plus or minus.
Paths are relative and allow those characters, spaces and slash.
Empty, dot and parent path components are forbidden.
Tabs, newlines, backslashes and other characters are unsupported.
.Pp
Directories are containers only.
Symlinks, hard-linked files and special files are unsupported.
Set-ID and sticky mode bits are rejected.
Owner/group, ACLs, extended attributes, directory modes, empty directories and
configuration semantics are not recorded.
Readable content is required even if its recorded permissions are otherwise valid.
.Sh WORLD AND DEPENDENCIES
The world file and registration dependency input contain one exact package name
per line, blank lines, or full-line comments beginning with #.
Do not indent names or add inline comments.
Duplicate names are rejected and order is immaterial.
Unknown world roots and dangling dependencies block inspection.
Dependency input is canonicalized during registration; world is not rewritten.
.Pp
List output labels world members explicit and all other packages dependency,
including unrooted orphan packages.
Orphan reporting follows the transitive dependency closure of world, including
cycles, and reports candidates without deleting them.
.Sh VERIFICATION AND RECOVERY
Verification checks only registered package stages and never repairs files.
Missing, changed, unreadable, unowned or unsupported entries fail verification.
Invalid records and graphs fail before payload inspection and produce no partial
inspection or orphan results.
Files outside registered stages are not inventoried.
.Pp
Identical registration is idempotent; changed evidence for an existing name is
rejected.
A validated record is published through an adjacent temporary copy and rename.
This is not a multi-record transaction or power-loss durability guarantee.
Pending replacement guards normal operations.
Use the separately pinned replacement procedure; do not repair a pending record
by editing it to match the desired outcome.
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
Legacy pkg-state-v1 uses four fields in file rows and records no mode.
It remains inspectable, but verification reports mode-untracked and fails for
its files.
No migration infers trusted permissions from possibly changed payloads.
Use a fresh private root for new registration and v2 transport.
Mixed-version inspection is supported; binary export requires full verification.
.Sh EXAMPLES
After following the hello-local registration example in
.Xr pkg-mgr 1 ,
set the requested root and inspect it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf 'hello-local\en' > "$root/state/world"
bin/pkg-mgr --root "$root" list
bin/pkg-mgr --root "$root" --format tsv orphans
.Ed
.Pp
The list labels hello-local explicit.
The orphan report has its non-deleting header and no orphan rows.
The write changes only the world file in the disposable example root.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa state/packages/NAME.tsv
Generated package record.
.It Pa state/world
Editable requested roots.
.It Pa stage/NAME
The corresponding staged payload.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg-mgr 1
.Pp
See docs/PACKAGE-STATE.md for helper commands and validation context,
docs/REPLACEMENT-POLICY.md for replacement, and docs/BINARY-PACKAGE.md for
transport binding.
